# Batch files MUST be CRLF.
#
# cmd.exe mis-parses a multi-line `( ... )` block in an LF-only .bat: it
# executes fragments of the block's own lines as commands and skips the rest.
# `deploy.bat` was checked in with LF and failed exactly that way — steps 1-4
# (dependencies, typecheck, production build) printed nothing at all and the
# script went straight to the push prompt. A gate that silently does not run is
# worse than no gate: it would have pushed a broken build to production.
#
# Found 2026-08-31 while running the 0.3.3 deploy. `eol=crlf` is what stops a
# clone or a checkout from putting it back.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
